node_modules/
dist/
# The built drive CLI binary. `go build ./...` in the repo root writes ./drive;
# it is a build artifact, never committed. The pattern is anchored to the repo
# root: a bare `drive` also ignored the cmd/drive source directory, so a new
# file there was added to the working tree and silently left out of the commit.
/drive
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars
.wrangler/
.cloudflare/

# The Windows installer (drive#154): the built drive.exe, the vendor's
# rclone.exe, WinFsp's MSI and the MSI and bundle built from installer/*.wxs
# are all build artifacts of .github/workflows/windows-msi.yml, never committed. The
# sources beside them are.
/installer/drive.exe
/installer/rclone.exe
/installer/winfsp.msi
/installer/drive.msi
/installer/drive-setup.exe
# Lighthouse CI's run artefacts (drive#225): the reports are the run's output,
# and `git status` and a release should not carry them. The budgets live in
# lighthouserc.json, which is committed.
.lighthouseci/

# Go CLI
/drive
/cmd/drive/drive
*.test

# The docs site (issue #98): generated, never committed. `npm run docs:build`
# renders the {{MARKER}}s from src/billing.js into docs-site/.rendered and
# builds the HTML, the per-page .md copies and llms.txt / llms-full.txt into
# public/docs, which is the Worker's static asset directory.
docs-site/.rendered/
public/docs/

# Inspect eval logs (evals/agents) stay out of the repository.
logs/
docsbuild.done
docsbuild.log
